{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1744166,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"Soap Making","festival_id":504454,"organization_id":675999,"web_url":"www.techfest26.com\/","start_date":"2026-09-02T18:30:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-17T10:30:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/soap-making-techfest26-annual-technical-festival-of-sliet-sant-longowal-institute-of-engineering-and-techno-1744166","region":"online","details":"<p><strong>All That You Need to Know About Soap Making &mdash; techFEST'26<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>About techFEST'26<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>techFEST'26 is North India's premier technical festival, organised by Sant Longowal Institute of Engineering and Technology (SLIET), Longowal, Punjab.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Registration for the&nbsp;techFEST&rsquo;26 package&nbsp;is compulsory for&nbsp;accommodation and&nbsp;other perks, while&nbsp;participation in individual&nbsp;events is free*.<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><a href=\"http:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\">www.techfest26.com<\/a><\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Register Now:<\/strong><br \/><a href=\"https:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/package\">https:\/\/www.techFEST26.com\/package<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Website and Email:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Website: <a href=\"http:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\">www.techfest26.com<\/a><\/li>\n<li>Email: <a href=\"mailto:techfest@sliet.ac.in\">techfest@sliet.ac.in<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Follow Us for Updates:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Instagram and other social media platforms<\/p>\n<p><strong>For Queries:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Naman Kumar Sinha (Overall Coordinator): +91 78568 93952<\/li>\n<li>Shubham Kumar Singh (Overall Coordinator): +91 97711 74465<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Prepare yourself for a journey of technology, creativity, and celebration.<\/p>\n<p>Mark your calendars and be part of the magic of techFEST'26 at SLIET.<\/p>\n<p>We cordially invite you to Soap Making, organised as part of <strong>techFEST'26<\/strong> - Annual Technical Festival of SLIET. Showcase your talent, compete with the sharpest minds and earn your moment of glory.<\/p>\n<p><strong>&ldquo;From Ingredients to Innovation: Unveiling the Art of Soap Making&rdquo;.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>About the Event:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Soap making is an event where participants delve into the world of fragrance and skincare as they perform and present the intricate processes behind soap production.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Task for Team:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Evaluate soap making based on the following criteria:<\/p>\n<p><strong>Soap:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>pH maintain<\/li>\n<li>Foam quality (tested through a foam test)<\/li>\n<li>Performance in both hard and soft water<\/li>\n<li>The sample weight should be 80-100g<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Event Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Number of rounds: 3<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Abstract Submission<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Format of the abstract: Title, Participant's Name, Email, Mobile No., College Name, Branch, Registration No.<\/li>\n<li>Abstract (1-2 pages): The abstract must have an appropriate title, picture &amp; overview of the topic.<\/li>\n<li>The full paper margin line is 1.5 cm.<\/li>\n<li>The abstract must be submitted as a hard copy, a week before the presentation.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Question and Answer Session<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>3-minute Question and Answer session.<\/li>\n<li>Participants are required to submit their presentation in .pptx format to the event head before the start of the event.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 3: Sample and Testing<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>At the time of presentation, participants are required to be present with the sample soap and a printed form of their abstract or flow sheet or poster.<\/li>\n<li>The sample must be visually appealing.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Judgment Criteria:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Stage 1: Abstract (Weightage 30%)<\/li>\n<li>Stage 2: Question and Answer Session (Weightage 30%)<\/li>\n<li>Stage 3: Sample and Testing (Weightage 40%)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; FAQs:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team should have at least two members.<\/li>\n<li>Each participating team should have a unique name.<\/li>\n<li>All undergraduate and diploma students with valid ID cards of their respective educational institutes are allowed to participate.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the judges will be final and binding.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Certification Policy:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Certificates will be provided to all the participants.<\/li>\n<li>Certificate of Excellence will be provided to the winners (as per the results declared by the judges).<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Important Note:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All the participants must make payment on the techFEST'26 website. Without payment, their participation will not be considered, and they will be disqualified.<\/li>\n<li>The organizers reserve the right to modify the rules, prize pool, dates, venue, or timing of the competition if deemed necessary under unforeseen circumstances.<\/li>\n<li>All guidelines are subject to change. Participants are advised to regularly check the official techFEST'26 website for any updates. Any changes or announcements will be posted there. Adherence to the latest rules is mandatory for all teams.<\/li>\n<li><strong>The details mentioned in this Problem Statement may be subject to change at any time.<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>For Further Query:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Domain Advisor:<\/strong> Sahil Sinha, 2432067\/GCT, 9065297749<\/li>\n<li><strong>Domain Coordinator:<\/strong> Amit Kumar, 254013105\/GCT, 8010064068<\/li>\n<li><strong>Event Coordinator:<\/strong> Atul Raj, 254014030\/GCT, 6203500824<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules and Regulations - General Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All participants must carry a valid college ID card and their techFEST'26 registration receipt.<\/li>\n<li>Reporting time will be communicated to registered teams; late reporting may lead to walkover.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the judges and organisers will be final and binding in all matters.<\/li>\n<li>Any form of misconduct, plagiarism or use of unfair means leads to immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Participants are responsible for their own equipment and personal belongings.<\/li>\n<li>Organisers reserve the right to modify any rule at any time; updates are announced at the venue.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to students of all institutes and all degree programmes (unless specified otherwise in the event rules above).<\/li>\n<li>Participants must be registered for techFEST'26 through the official portal.<\/li>\n<li>Cross-college teams are welcome.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Mark your calendars and be part of the magic of techFEST'26 at SLIET!<\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27463276,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-08-25T20:39:52+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-01T23:09:12+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"6cwxFE1","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":70,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-08-27 03:52:27","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_autom